<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I ran my RT90 (supposedly with GPS) for several hours on my dashboard and it never "saw" a single hint of a satellite <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_cry.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":cry:" title="Crying or Very Sad"> <br>Is it possible that I was shipped a non-GPS radio?<br>Can the radio even detect whether it has a GPS?<br>My RT3S with GPS works fine on that dash - even works indoors <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_eek.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":shock:" title="Shocked"></div></blockquote>If OpenGD77 detects NMEA data on the GPS input to the MCU during startup it presume that a GPS chip is attached and<br>enables the possibility to enabled it in options.<br>So , you have something in the radio that at least think it is an GPS.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Tue Dec 05, 2023 8:51 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
